# Microsoft Enterprise TypeScript Conventions

## Enterprise Code Style

### Enterprise-Strict TypeScript

- Always use strict mode (enabled in tsconfig.json) - Microsoft enterprise standard
- No implicit `any` types - Enterprise type safety requirement
- Explicit return types on all functions - Enterprise code clarity
- Use interfaces over type aliases when possible - Enterprise maintainability
- **Microsoft TypeScript guidelines** compliance required

### Naming Conventions

- **Files**: camelCase (e.g., `sttService.ts`, `webhookController.ts`)
- **Classes**: PascalCase (e.g., `STTService`, `LLMService`)
- **Functions**: camelCase (e.g., `transcribe()`, `generateResponse()`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `OPENAI_CONFIG`, `MAX_FILE_SIZE`)
- **Interfaces**: PascalCase (e.g., `Config`, `ConversationMessage`)
- **Types**: PascalCase (e.g., `TTSVoice`, `LogLevel`)

### Import Order

```typescript
// 1. External dependencies
import express from 'express';
import { Bot } from 'grammy';

// 2. Internal dependencies (config, services, utils)
import { config } from '../config/env';
import { openai } from '../config/openai';
import { sttService } from '../services/stt.service';

// 3. Types
import { ConversationMessage } from '../types';

// 4. Utilities
import { logger } from '../utils/logger';
```

## Async/Await Best Practices

### Always Use Async/Await

```typescript
// ✅ Good
async function processMessage(text: string): Promise<string> {
  const response = await llmService.generateResponse(text);
  return response;
}

// ❌ Bad - don't use callbacks
function processMessage(text: string, callback: (response: string) => void) {
  llmService.generateResponse(text).then(callback);
}
```

### Avoid Return Await

```typescript
// ✅ Good - return promise directly
async function getData(): Promise<Data> {
  return fetchData();
}

// ❌ Bad - unnecessary await
async function getData(): Promise<Data> {
  return await fetchData();
}
```

### Exception: Use await when in try-catch

```typescript
// ✅ Good - await needed for error handling
async function getData(): Promise<Data> {
  try {
    return await fetchData();
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error('Failed', { error });
    throw new CustomError('Error');
  }
}
```

## Error Handling

### Use Custom Error Classes

```typescript
// ✅ Good
import { STTError } from '../utils/errorHandler';

try {
  const result = await transcribe(file);
} catch (error) {
  throw new STTError(`Transcription failed: ${error.message}`);
}
```

### Always Log Errors with Context

```typescript
// ✅ Good
catch (error) {
  logger.error('Operation failed', {
    operation: 'transcribe',
    filePath,
    error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),
  });
  throw new STTError('Transcription failed');
}

// ❌ Bad - no context
catch (error) {
  throw new Error('Failed');
}
```

## Function Signatures

### Always Specify Return Types

```typescript
// ✅ Good
async function transcribe(audioPath: string): Promise<string> {
  // ...
}

function formatLog(level: string, message: string): string {
  // ...
}

// ❌ Bad - missing return type
async function transcribe(audioPath: string) {
  // ...
}
```

### Use Readonly for Non-Mutated Properties

```typescript
// ✅ Good
class ConversationStore {
  private readonly conversations = new Map<number, Message[]>();
}

// ❌ Bad
class ConversationStore {
  private conversations = new Map<number, Message[]>();
}
```

## Type Safety

### Use Type Guards

```typescript
// ✅ Good
if (error instanceof AppError) {
  return handleOperationalError(error);
}

if (typeof response === 'string') {
  return response.trim();
}
```

### Use Union Types for Known Values

```typescript
// ✅ Good
type VideoStyle = 'waveform' | 'simple' | 'branded';
type TTSVoice = 'alloy' | 'echo' | 'fable' | 'onyx' | 'nova' | 'shimmer';

// ❌ Bad
type VideoStyle = string;
```

### Use Interfaces for Object Shapes

```typescript
// ✅ Good
interface ProcessingStats {
  downloadDuration?: number;
  sttDuration?: number;
  llmDuration?: number;
  totalDuration: number;
}

// ❌ Bad
type ProcessingStats = {
  downloadDuration: number | undefined;
  // ...
};
```

## Logging

### Always Include Context

```typescript
// ✅ Good
logger.info('Processing message', {
  chatId,
  userId,
  messageType: 'text',
  textLength: text.length,
});

// ❌ Bad
logger.info('Processing message');
```

### Use Appropriate Log Levels

```typescript
logger.error('Critical failure', { error }); // For errors
logger.warn('Potential issue', { data }); // For warnings
logger.info('Normal operation', { stats }); // For info
logger.debug('Detailed debug', { details }); // For debug
```

## File Operations

### Always Clean Up Files

```typescript
// ✅ Good
const filesToCleanup: string[] = [];
try {
  const file1 = await createFile();
  filesToCleanup.push(file1);

  const file2 = await processFile(file1);
  filesToCleanup.push(file2);

  return file2;
} catch (error) {
  throw error;
} finally {
  await mediaService.deleteFiles(filesToCleanup);
}
```

### Use Utility Functions

```typescript
// ✅ Good - use provided utilities
import { getTempFilePath, deleteFile } from '../utils/fileUtils';

const filePath = getTempFilePath('mp3');

// ❌ Bad - don't create custom path logic
const filePath = `tmp/${Date.now()}.mp3`;
```

## Configuration

### Use Environment Config

```typescript
// ✅ Good
import { config } from '../config/env';

const port = config.port;
const apiKey = config.openai.apiKey;

// ❌ Bad - don't access process.env directly
const port = process.env.PORT;
```

### Use OpenAI Config Constants

```typescript
// ✅ Good
import { OPENAI_CONFIG } from '../config/openai';

const response = await openai.audio.transcriptions.create({
  model: OPENAI_CONFIG.whisper.model,
  language: OPENAI_CONFIG.whisper.language,
});

// ❌ Bad - hardcoded values
const response = await openai.audio.transcriptions.create({
  model: 'whisper-1',
  language: 'en',
});
```

## Service Pattern

### Export Singleton Instance

```typescript
// ✅ Good
export class STTService {
  async transcribe(audioPath: string): Promise<string> {
    // ...
  }
}

export const sttService = new STTService();

// Usage: import { sttService } from '../services/stt.service';
```

### Method Structure

```typescript
async methodName(param: Type): Promise<ReturnType> {
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    logger.info('Operation started', { param });

    // Validation
    if (!param) {
      throw new CustomError('Invalid param');
    }

    // Main logic
    const result = await doSomething(param);

    // Success logging
    const duration = Date.now() - startTime;
    logger.info('Operation completed', { duration, result });

    return result;
  } catch (error) {
    const duration = Date.now() - startTime;
    logger.error('Operation failed', { duration, error });
    throw new CustomError(`Operation failed: ${error.message}`);
  }
}
```

## FFmpeg Callbacks

### Type FFmpeg Callbacks

```typescript
// ✅ Good - explicitly type callbacks
ffmpeg(inputPath)
  .on('start', (command: string) => {
    logger.debug('FFmpeg started', { command });
  })
  .on('error', (error: Error) => {
    logger.error('FFmpeg failed', { error: error.message });
    reject(error);
  })
  .on('end', () => {
    logger.info('FFmpeg completed');
    resolve(outputPath);
  });
```

## Don'ts

### Don't Use Classes for Everything

```typescript
// ❌ Bad - unnecessary class
class Utils {
  static formatDate(date: Date): string {
    return date.toISOString();
  }
}

// ✅ Good - simple function
export function formatDate(date: Date): string {
  return date.toISOString();
}
```

### Don't Use Builder Pattern

```typescript
// ❌ Bad - avoid returning 'this'
class Builder {
  setProperty(value: string): this {
    this.property = value;
    return this;
  }
}

// ✅ Good - separate functions
function setProperty(obj: Object, value: string): void {
  obj.property = value;
}
```

### Don't Use console.log Directly

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
console.log('Message processed');

// ✅ Good - use logger
logger.info('Message processed', { chatId });
```

## Performance Tips

### Avoid Unnecessary Awaits

```typescript
// ✅ Good - parallel execution
const [result1, result2] = await Promise.all([operation1(), operation2()]);

// ❌ Bad - sequential execution
const result1 = await operation1();
const result2 = await operation2();
```

### Use Appropriate Data Structures

```typescript
// ✅ Good - Map for lookups
const conversations = new Map<number, Message[]>();

// ❌ Bad - Array for lookups
const conversations: Array<{ id: number; messages: Message[] }> = [];
```

## Testing Considerations

### Write Testable Code

```typescript
// ✅ Good - dependency injection friendly
export function createService(openaiClient: OpenAI) {
  return {
    async transcribe(file: string) {
      return openaiClient.audio.transcriptions.create(/*...*/);
    },
  };
}

// ❌ Bad - hard to test
import { openai } from '../config/openai';
export function transcribe(file: string) {
  return openai.audio.transcriptions.create(/*...*/);
}
```
